This is an outline of what Luis helped me figure out, for general consumption:

**this is using the current dev version of dartR (Version 2.3.3)

1. Download newhybrids from https://github.com/green-striped-gecko/dartR/tree/master/binaries
2. Place newhybrids IN the folder that is your working directory. The process does not work if newhybrids is in a different directory. This is because newhybrids is trying to look at files that are in the same folder as itself. You can either make lots of copies of newhybrids in your working folders, or change the working directory to where newhybrids is stored. Option two means your newhybrids outputs will be written to this new directory, obviously.
3. Run newhybrids via the r code :

m <- gl.nhybrids(testset.gl <http://testset.gl/>, outfile='nhyb.txt',
                 p0=NULL, p1=NULL,
                 nhyb.directory=getwd(),
                 BurnIn=100,
                 sweeps=100,
                 verbose=3)

Some errors and how to resolve them:

Permission denied issues (i.e "sh: /path_to_file/newhybs: Permission denied") can be resolved in terminal with the command:
chmod 755 path_to_file/newhybs

If you have any spaces anywhere in your path name you will fail. Newhybrids does not understand spaces in path names.

